<title>USA: P&amp;G declines comment on Snapple, Gatorade.</title>
<headline>P&amp;G declines comment on Snapple, Gatorade.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co declined comment Friday on a published report that it may be interested in buying Quaker Oats Co's biggest business, its Gatorade sports drink line, or its Snapple beverage line.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no news to report,&quot; P&amp;G spokeswoman Lisa Jester said in a telephone interview. &quot;We can't comment on speculation.&quot;</p>
<p>The Wall Street Journal's &quot;Heard on the Street&quot; column said Friday that P&amp;G or others could be interested if the cereal maker sold its beverage business. Quaker has also declined comment on whether it is seeking a buyer.</p>
<p>((-- Susan Zimmerman, Cleveland Newsdesk 216-579-0077))</p>
